      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Sanctuary of Pachacámac in Lurín once housed two large oval temples built around 200 B.C., drawing pilgrims from afar.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scribd.com/document/922545186/Historical-Review-of-Lurin",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From 700 A.D. to 1,200 A.D., Lurín reached a cultural peak marked by pyramids and strong Wari influence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scribd.com/document/922545186/Historical-Review-of-Lurin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "When the Spanish arrived in 1533, they imposed encomiendas that reshaped Lurín’s social and economic landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scribd.com/document/922545186/Historical-Review-of-Lurin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A tsunami in 1687 destroyed the town of Quilcay, prompting its residents to relocate and found San Pedro de Lurín.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
